        {
            "id": "14098339",
            "user": "75.112.161.130",
            "timestamp": "19:47, 1 July 2014",
            "anon": true,
            "size": "(7,695 bytes)",
            "change": 0,
            "summary": "",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "adjustment",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "Most of us probably think that flour is cultivated somewhere by elves that work long hours in a factory. The truth of the matter is that you can make it yourself in ''seconds''. Why use that processed junk that's been losing vitamins for weeks on the shelves when you can get the good stuff now? All you need is some sort of grain that can be used as a flour, and a grinding apparatus (such as a coffee grinder or a coffee mill."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "Most of us probably think that flour is cultivated somewhere by elves that work long hours in a factory. The truth of the matter is that you can make it yourself in ''seconds''. Why use that processed crap that's been losing vitamins for weeks on the shelves when you can get the good stuff now? All you need is some sort of grain that can be used as a flour, and a grinding apparatus (such as a coffee grinder or a coffee mill."
                ]
            }
        },
