        {
            "id": "9050301",
            "user": "Melwade",
            "timestamp": "10:32, 17 January 2013",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(3,410 bytes)",
            "change": 3388,
            "summary": "(Reverted edits by 122.57.11.176 (Talk); changed back to last version by Votebot)",
            "is_minor": true,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "reverted",
            "contribution_type": "revert",
            "reverted_by": "JuneDays",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "[[Image:Wheatfield   Lillehammer, Norway 4333.jpg|thumb|200px|right|Norwegian wheat field.]]<BR>",
                    "",
                    "Making flour is not for the faint of heart. It is a long, ongoing process in which the wheat is planted, later [[Grow Your Own Food|harvested]], and then ground to make flour.The earliest methods used for producing flour all involved grinding grain between stones. Below are the steps needed to make flour.",
                    "[[Category:Baking]]",
                    "== Steps ==",
                    "===Planting===",
                    "#  Purchase wheat [[Winter Sow Seeds Outdoors|seeds]]. Search catalogs or head to the natural food store to purchase seeds.",
                    "#  [[Find Free Compost Ingredients|Amend soil]], if needed. Wheat seeds need to be planted in a rich soil.",
                    "#  Plant wheat seed.",
                    "===Cultivation===",
                    "#  [[Fertilize a Garden Cheaply|Fertilize]] crop as required.",
                    "#  [[Start an Organic Garden|Weed]] as needed.",
                    "===Harvest===",
                    "#  Cut the wheat using a scythe or other [[Sharpen a Knife|sharp knife]].",
                    "#  Tie the cut wheat into bundles.",
                    "#  Thresh the wheat by taking a handful of  wheat and beating it against the interior of a barrel or other hard surface. The [[Brew Beer Using All Grain Method|grain]] will fall off the stalks. Discard the stalks.",
                    "#  Remove (Winnow) the wheat from the chaff. To separate the wheat from the chaff toss the wheat from one container to another allowing airflow to remove the wheat from the chaff. Wind or a fan can be used for this purpose.",
                    "===Storage===",
                    "#  Store the dry wheat in an [[Store a Christmas Cake|airtight]] container. Make sure wheat does not become damp or it will spoil.",
                    "===Flour===",
                    "#  Grind <ref>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mill_%28grinding%29 Wikipedia article on grinding wheat</ref> the wheat using a mill. Mills can be either hand cranked or electric.[[Image:Hammer mill open front full 2993.jpg|thumb|150[x|right|Hammer Mill.]]",
                    "#  [[Sift Flour|Sift]] the wheat to remove bits of whole grain, if desired. <ref>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flour Wikipedia's article about Flour.</ref>",
                    "",
                    "== Tips ==",
                    "*Note there are different types of wheat based on protein content. Red or winter wheat is normally used for baking breads.",
                    "*Soft wheat is normally used to make cakes and pastries.",
                    "*All-purpose (plain) flour is a combination of both hard and soft flours. It is used for baking both breads and cakes.",
                    "",
                    "== Warnings ==",
                    "",
                    "*Wheat flour is flammable. Wheat mills have been known to explode or catch on  fire from just a spark.",
                    "*Wheat is prone to toxins <ref>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ergot Wikipedia Ergot</ref> so use care when growing, harvesting and storing wheat.",
                    "",
                    "== Related wikiHows ==",
                    "*[[Make an All Purpose Gluten Free Flour|How to Make an All Purpose Gluten Free Flour]]",
                    "*[[Harvest Wheat|How to Harvest Wheat]]",
                    "*  [[Make Organic Plant Food|How to Make Organic Plant Food]]",
                    "*  [[Practice Sustainable Agriculture|How to Practice Sustainable Agriculture]]",
                    "*  [[Become a Farmer Without Experience|How to Become a Farmer Without Experience]]",
                    "*  [[Get Started in Crop Rotation|How to Get Started in Crop Rotation]]",
                    "*  [[Plow With Two Row Cultivators|How to Plow With Two Row Cultivators]]",
                    "*  [[Calibrate a Sprayer|How to Calibrate a Sprayer]]",
                    "*  [[Grow Heirloom Tomatoes|How to Grow Heirloom Tomatoes]]",
                    "*[[Make Cake Flour|How to Make Cake Flour]]",
                    "",
                    "",
                    "== Sources and Citations ==",
                    "*http://www.breadinfo.com/floura.shtml",
                    "*http://www.cookingforengineers.com/article/63/Wheat-Flour",
                    "*http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flour",
                    "{{reflist}}",
                    "",
                    "",
                    "[[es:hacer harina]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "THIS IS LIEING ITS GAY"
                ]
            }
        },
